# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary safety for the payload under data/.
#
# This is insurance against a margin, not a fix for a present bug. Measured
# with tools/check_package.py, all 28 buffers are correctly classified as
# binary by Git as they stand, and a round trip through a repo with
# core.autocrlf=true returns every one of them byte-identical.
#
# The margin is worth naming, because one file's safety is thinner than the
# rest. Git's is_binary() in convert.c, which is what governs CRLF rewriting,
# accepts a file as binary on either of two grounds: a NUL byte, or the ratio
# test (printable >> 7) < nonprintable. Twenty-seven buffers carry NUL bytes
# and are safe on the first ground. level0_rgb.bin contains no NUL at all --
# it is 150000 uint8 RGB triplets -- and is safe only on the second, by
# 9849 nonprintable bytes against a threshold of 3435.
#
# That threshold is a property of the pixel values, not of the format. A
# re-export with a lighter colour ramp would carry fewer bytes below 32, and
# if the count fell under about 3500 the file would flip to "text". Git would
# then rewrite its line endings on add and on checkout, shift every RGB
# triplet after the first CR-LF pair, and the cloud would render with
# corrupted colours. Nothing would warn you; the page would still load.
#
# The rules below remove that dependency on the data. data/checksums.sha256
# detects the failure if these rules are ever dropped:
#     python tools/check_package.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Normalise line endings for genuine text, so the repo stays LF-in, native-out.
* text=auto

# Never touch these, whatever the heuristic decides.
*.bin  binary
*.h5   binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary

# The vendored Plotly build is third-party. Excluding it from GitHub's language
# statistics stops a 4.5 MB minified bundle from reporting this as a
# JavaScript project, and collapses it in pull request diffs.
vendor/** linguist-vendored
vendor/** -diff

# Generated payload, not authored source: keep it out of the language stats and
# out of diffs, where a raw buffer is noise.
data/*.bin linguist-generated
